{
  "heading": "A route receives the caller's identity, in every Yon language",
  "axis": "language",
  "summary": "Mark a route parameter FromIdentity, and the method receives the object that your identity provider returned for this request, as an ordinary model. Only a @SignedIn or @Allow route can take it, one per method, and the identity provider is still called once per request (ADR NNNN).",
  "body": "Choose a language below. `MeController` says `SignedIn`, and its method `getMe` takes one parameter marked `FromIdentity`, of the model `Identity` with the fields `user` and `roles`. It returns the caller's user name. `AppIdentityProvider` and the role `Admin` are the same as in the example above. With the header `authorization: ada-token`, `GET /me` answers `\"ada\"`; with `bob-token`, `\"bob\"`; without the header, 401, and the method does not run.\n\nThe model must name every field that `identify` returns, as a body model must. If the identity does not fit the model, the server answers the fixed 500 `Handler execution failed. Reference: <id>.` (the built-in case `UnexpectedError`) and logs `route.identity_mismatch` with the request id and the route, never the identity's values. The build refuses `FromIdentity` on a `@Public` route (the rule on the method wins), a second `FromIdentity` parameter, and `FromIdentity` on an identity provider, a worker or a socket method. The identity is not part of `/api.json` or the `OPTIONS` schema.",
